pysisyphus 1.0.0: 0001-gs-bofill-update

What: Gonzalez–Schlegel micro-steps update the Hessian with Bofill instead of BFGS (BFGS is unstable where a curvature is negative, as in the flat tails); the update is skipped for a zero step.
Test: Replay of the recorded first step of tail_gs_reactant (before the fixes; tests/test_pysisyphus_patches.py): BFGS turns the lowest curvature from −0.0152 to −0.621 au, as in the run; Bofill (with 0002) gives −0.0027 au.

--- a/pysisyphus/irc/GonzalezSchlegel.py
+++ b/pysisyphus/irc/GonzalezSchlegel.py
@@ -4,7 +4,7 @@
 from scipy.optimize import newton
 
 from pysisyphus.irc.IRC import IRC
-from pysisyphus.optimizers.hessian_updates import bfgs_update
+from pysisyphus.optimizers.hessian_updates import bofill_update
 
 
 # [1] An improved algorithm for reaction path following
@@ -94,9 +94,9 @@
             and (self.micro_counter % self.hessian_recalc == 0)
         ):
             self.mw_hessian = self.geometry.mw_hessian
-        # Or update Hessian
-        else:
-            dH, _ = bfgs_update(self.mw_hessian, coords_diff, gradient_diff)
+        # Or update Hessian (Bofill: stable where a curvature is negative; no update for a zero step)
+        elif np.linalg.norm(coords_diff) > 1e-10:
+            dH, _ = bofill_update(self.mw_hessian, coords_diff, gradient_diff)
             self.mw_hessian += dH
         eigvals, eigvecs = np.linalg.eigh(self.mw_hessian)
 
